WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.860
Second speaker is someone who understands

2
00:00:01.860 --> 00:00:04.100
that lasting success is built through discipline,

3
00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:06.420
consistency, and continuous improvement.

4
00:00:07.520 --> 00:00:09.960
Mike has spent 37 years as a martial artist,

5
00:00:10.360 --> 00:00:12.540
training in karate, kickboxing, and jiu-jitsu.

6
00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:15.440
So Kaizen is a Japanese word

7
00:00:15.440 --> 00:00:17.000
that means continuous improvement.

8
00:00:17.370 --> 00:00:19.250
He said, you're the only recruiter in Raleigh

9
00:00:19.250 --> 00:00:21.750
that I know that will turn out a high five figure thing.

10
00:00:21.790 --> 00:00:23.990
Cause I know you'd get a decent amount of money out of this.

11
00:00:24.650 --> 00:00:26.590
And I said, well, integrity is more important

12
00:00:26.590 --> 00:00:27.050
than the placement.

13
00:00:27.270 --> 00:00:29.030
The relationship is more important than the placement.

14
00:00:29.430 --> 00:00:31.410
And I think you gotta be passionate in everything you do.

15
00:00:31.910 --> 00:00:33.110
And that's whether it's professionally

16
00:00:33.110 --> 00:00:34.170
or whether it's personally.

17
00:00:34.650 --> 00:00:36.130
You gotta find what you wanna do.

18
00:00:36.530 --> 00:00:38.350
And whatever that is, you gotta be all in.

19
00:00:38.630 --> 00:00:39.630
And I think a lot of times,

20
00:00:39.630 --> 00:00:42.470
energy management is more important than time management.

21
00:00:42.770 --> 00:00:45.190
99 times out of 100, the things that are gonna be put

22
00:00:45.190 --> 00:00:47.210
in front of you are not good.

23
00:00:47.990 --> 00:00:50.590
But you've gotta be wary, you've gotta be discretionary,

24
00:00:51.230 --> 00:00:52.590
and you've gotta be agile and know

25
00:00:52.590 --> 00:00:53.870
when to jump from that opportunity

26
00:00:53.870 --> 00:00:55.170
and give it everything you've got.

27
00:00:55.350 --> 00:00:57.370
Because they come along so sparingly in life.

28
00:00:57.620 --> 00:00:59.700
I would ask you to introspectively look at yourself

29
00:00:59.700 --> 00:01:00.840
at who you are today

30
00:01:01.360 --> 00:01:03.720
and what do you have to do to close the gap

31
00:01:03.720 --> 00:01:05.380
to be a better version of yourself tomorrow?

32
00:01:06.160 --> 00:01:07.280
Thank you guys so much.

33
00:01:07.700 --> 00:01:08.020
It was an honor.

